{
  "sticker": "clam",
  "skeleton": "clam facing the viewer: root on the ground under the shell; body with a belly bone (squash); lid: the top shell, pivot at the hinge behind the bottom shell, stretched down to close and lifted to open; the soft body and the pearl between the shells (opening, the soft body swells up with the pearl on it — the sheet's separate 'inside' oval is not used: drawn over the top shell it read as a second clam); the bottom shell in front carries the face (eyes, brows, mouth).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling clam character. Draw this exact clam as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the top shell: the big fan-shaped upper shell with its scalloped pink-and-cream ribs, as in image 1, alone, drawn whole, including its lower part and hinge normally hidden behind the lower shell.\n2. the bottom shell: the lower shell with its wavy rim and ribs, facing the viewer as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no brows, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks.\n3. the soft body: the pale cream soft body of the clam that shows between its two shells in image 1, drawn whole as a soft rounded oval.\n4. the inside of the open shell: the glossy, deep coral-pink inside of the clam, a wide rounded oval, as seen when the shell opens wide.\n5. the pearl: a small round shiny white pearl with a soft pink sheen.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or another part) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a smiling clam character; image 2 shows the same clam cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the clam's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the clam in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a big dark brown eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the same eye squeezed shut, crying: a tight, creased, downward-curving closed line.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile line.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n11. the mouth open in a wobbly crying wail, its corners turned down, the inside pink.\n12. one eyebrow as in image 1: a small, thin, softly curved dark brown line.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
